      "writtenOn": "2023-06-14T18:52:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I like the idea of having a function to compose VDM headers, but this macro usage is getting pretty convoluted. I\u0027d prefer to refactor existing usage than add another way of doing the same thing.\n\n1. See my above comment about refactoring `pd_get_vdo_ver` to deal with the minor version.\n2. AFAICT, the `VDO` macro is only used to compose VDM headers, but as you\u0027ve noticed, it\u0027s awkward for that. I think we could entirely replace it with a function like this. It would be nice if you did that, but if you don\u0027t feel like it, could you declare this function in `usb_pd.h` to make the refactor easier later.\n3. If you do that, you\u0027ll need to pass in `tx_type` as an argument to make it stateless.\n\nNits:\n1. Please put the `port` argument first to align with the other functions in the TCPM.\n2. You should mask `cmd` with `VDO_CMDT_MASK`.",
      "revId": "cbe321c1502d127cb9060bbdb9bb8979bef15d08",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
